# Docker Environment Management

## CRITICAL: Do NOT kill arbitrary Docker containers or environments

When managing Docker containers in this project:

1. **ONLY** stop/kill/remove containers created from the `androidworld:full_adb_agent` image
2. **NEVER** run broad commands like `docker kill $(docker ps -q)`, `docker stop $(docker ps -q)`, or `docker rm -f $(docker ps -aq)`
3. **NEVER** run `docker compose down` or `docker-compose down` without explicit user confirmation

## Safe commands (OK to use)

```bash
# Stop/kill only androidworld:full_adb_agent containers
docker ps -q --filter "ancestor=androidworld:full_adb_agent" | xargs -r docker stop
docker ps -q --filter "ancestor=androidworld:full_adb_agent" | xargs -r docker rm -f
```

## Forbidden commands (NEVER use)

```bash
# These kill ALL containers — DO NOT USE
docker kill $(docker ps -q)
docker stop $(docker ps -q)
docker rm -f $(docker ps -aq)
docker system prune
for i in $(seq 0 15); do docker rm -f env$i; done
```

## Before any Docker cleanup

Always use `docker ps --filter "ancestor=androidworld:full_adb_agent"` to list only relevant containers before stopping or removing them.
